      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMHO it is weird that `outputParseResult` is passed as an \"out\" argument and ParseShaderModule returns MaybeError.\n\nWhy can\u0027t ParseShaderModule return ResultOrError\u003csome result struct\u003e and then the result struct has `MaybeError CheckErrors()`. This would require storing the errors text in the cache but that\u0027s fine, it\u0027s just the compilation messages. So the code here would look like\n\n```\n           ShaderModuleParseRequest req \u003d BuildShaderModuleParseRequest(\n                    this, blueprint.GetHash(), unpacked, internalExtensions,\n                    /* needReflection */ true);\n\n                CacheResult\u003cShaderModuleParseResult\u003e cacheResult;\n                DAWN_TRY_LOAD_OR_RUN(cacheResult, this, std::move(req),\n                                     ParseShaderModule, \"ShaderModuleParsing\");\n\n                // The cache stores both success and error parse results, propagate errors that happenend during parsing now.\n\t\t*outputParseResult \u003d cacheResult.Acquire();\n\t\tDAWN_TRY(outputParseResult-\u003eCheckErrors());\n\n                // If created successfully, compilation messages are moved into the shader module.\n                // Otherwise, it is kept in *outputParseResult so that we can create an error shader\n                // module from it.\n                Ref\u003cShaderModuleBase\u003e shaderModule;\n                DAWN_TRY_ASSIGN(shaderModule, CreateShaderModuleImpl(unpacked, internalExtensions,\n                                                                     outputParseResult));\n                shaderModule-\u003eSetContentHash(blueprintHash);\n                return shaderModule;\n```",
